# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kept on disk, deliberately not published.
#
# This is a product repo. The studio-period record, the private thesis notes and
# the spent one-shot scripts all live in this working folder so the full history
# is in one place, but they are not part of what ships.
#
# Everything under docs/week07-09/ is also committed on the `team_02` branch of
# the studio repo (github.com/sclebow/AIA26_Studio), so it is recoverable there.
# docs/thesis/ and docs/marketing/build/ exist ONLY here — back them up.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Frozen studio deliverables: decks, faculty notes, session findings, benchmark
# renders, screenshots. The evergreen engineering content was rewritten into
# docs/reference/ (cli.md, models-and-benchmarks.md) and stays published.
docs/week07/
docs/week08/
docs/week09/

# Deck-authoring tooling: a reportlab script and the brand TTFs it embeds.
# Builds docs/week08/ above, so it goes with it. Fonts are under the SIL OFL.
docs/build_deck_week08.py
docs/fonts/

# Private thesis notes (north star, roadmap, drafts).
docs/thesis/

# Promo video intermediates and the silent cut (~52 MB). The scored 45 s cut
# stays committed as the product's walkthrough.
docs/marketing/build/
docs/marketing/sensi-45s-16x9.mp4

# Spent one-shot scripts. Their output is already baked into
# randomized_layouts/*.json (geometry fixes, furnishing) or into a deck slide
# that is no longer published (before/after renders). Nothing imports them.
python/fix_example_layouts.py
python/furnish_layouts.py
python/gen_before_after.py

# Real personal personas. personas/persona.json ships as a neutral demo profile;
# anything named persona.<who>.local.json is private and stays here.
personas/persona.*.local.json

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
